   Political Science at the University of Pennsylvania, where she has
   taught since 2001 (jflynch@sas.upenn.edu). Her research concerns the
   politics of inequality, social policy, and the economy in comparative
   perspective, with a focus on the countries of Western Europe and the
   United States. Cammett and Lynch contributed equally to the research
   design, analysis of results, and writing of the paper. Gavril Bilev is
   Assistant Professor in the Department of Political Science at Merrimack
   College (Gavril Bilev bilevg@merrimack.edu). He specializes in
   Comparative Politics, with a focus on issues pertaining to
   democratization and formal institutional design. He teaches courses in
   Comparative Politics, Research Methods, and related fields. Bilev
   carried out the statistical analysis and designed the graphical
   presentation of the results, as well as assisting with the preparation
   of the paper. Funding for this research has been graciously provided by
   the Christopher H. Browne Center for International Politics at the
   University of Pennsylvania, and the Political Science Department at
